If you’re blaming our fandom for calling out the disgusting actions of Mikee, Cianne, Robbie, and Raheel regarding their mockery of PWDs, then yes, we’ll gladly take that blame. We will never apologize for speaking up against something that should never have been treated as a joke in the first place. If standing up for what is right makes us the bad guys in your narrative, then so be it.

But if you weren’t even among those who called them out, perhaps it’s time to ask yourself why you’re more bothered by the people who spoke up than by the actions that prompted the backlash in the first place. Sometimes, the issue isn’t who’s making the noise, but what caused people to speak up.

